# Every file listed in MANIFEST.sha256 is sealed by the SHA-256 of its exact bytes.
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default and the GitHub Windows runner
# default), checkout rewrites LF to CRLF, every digest changes, and
# `sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256` fails on a file nobody edited. `-text` turns off
# line-ending conversion, so checkout writes the committed bytes on every platform.
# MANIFEST.sha256 is pinned too: a CRLF copy puts a carriage return on each path.
# Root-level paths start with "/" so they do not also match files in subfolders.
# Files outside the manifest (README, LICENSE, docs/, .github/) keep default handling.
/00-ABSTRACT.md -text
/ASEITY-CONFRONTATION.md -text
/CATALOG.md -text
/CONFERRED-EXISTENCE.txt -text
/CROSS-EXAMINATION.md -text
/DISSERTATION-PROSPECTUS.md -text
/INDEX.md -text
/MANIFEST.sha256 -text
/PRESENTATION.md -text
/SUTURE-TEST.md -text
/SYLLABUS.md -text
/THE-STRAIGHT-LINE.md -text
/THESIS.md -text
_front/** -text
conferred-existence/** -text
dissertation/** -text
papers/** -text
references/** -text
submission/** -text
